Llmpalooza adaptations of the pinned ExLlamaV3 sources (D-053, D-066), for the
files llmpalooza compiles (third_party/patches/exllamav3/0002-llmp-build.patch):

- util.cuh: cuda_check, gpu_assert, cublas_check and cublas_assert, which
  print and call exit() on an error, are removed. No compiled file uses
  them; llmpalooza's launchers return CUDA errors as values instead, and a
  served process never exits from inside a kernel library. They are inline
  code in a header, so a guard macro would not keep them out of a
  translation unit that reaches the header without it, or undefines it.
  Any later use fails to compile.
- quant/exl3_gemm_inner.cuh: the `register` storage class is dropped from
  four local arrays. It has no effect; it is ill-formed since C++17, and
  NVCC's front end rejects it with a Clang host compiler (upstream builds
  with GCC, which only warns). The kernels' SASS is unchanged (checked
  against the P0 reference's hashes, docs/licensing.md).

diff --git a/exllamav3/exllamav3_ext/quant/exl3_gemm_inner.cuh b/exllamav3/exllamav3_ext/quant/exl3_gemm_inner.cuh
